<title>MEXICO: FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen up to 19.13 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen up to 19.13 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen rising 76 basis points to 19.13 percent, and rates are also seen rising at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of nine dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     18.37	    19.13		   +76  bps</p>
<p>    9-DAY	20.49	    20.94		   +45  bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    21.85	    22.01		   +16  bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     23.17	    23.19		   + 2  bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 (2330 GMT)</p>
<p>((--Elena Vega, Mexico City newsroom 525 7289559))</p>
</text>
